<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Importance of Water – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 7th Grade (CEFR: A2.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> The Importance of Water</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> Clean Water Is Important Because...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Follow instructions for academic tasks or projects. Reading: Extract key facts and details from informational texts. Phonemic Awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by applying knowledge of basic syllabification rules when decoding two-syllable, three-syllable, or compound words.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can follow instructions related to water conservation (e.g., "We need to save water every day.")<br>Can extract key details from texts about the importance of water (e.g., "If we don't keep water clean, people will get sick. Clean water is important for health.")<br>Can demonstrate phonemic awareness by applying basic syllabification rules when decoding two-syllable, three-syllable, or compound words (e.g., "forecast," "important").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #e6f2f9;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 55%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 15%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher projects a short paragraph on the board that includes several vocabulary words from Lesson 1 (e.g., "save," "waste," "potable," "shortage"). Students read the paragraph silently and then work individually to circle all the words related to water that they remember. This activates prior reading knowledge and vocabulary. Example paragraph: "Water is an essential resource. We must learn to save it daily. If we waste water, we will face a shortage."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models reading the paragraph aloud with clear pronunciation and intonation. The teacher points to words like "essential" and "shortage" and quickly reviews their meanings, connecting them to prior learning. The teacher also explicitly models how to identify words related to water in the text.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the paragraph mainly about?" (Expected answer: "Water" or "Saving water.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can you find a word that means 'not enough water'?" (Expected answer: "shortage.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do we save water or waste water?" (Expected answer: "Save water.")</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An informational text (short article/poster) titled "Why Clean Water Matters" which highlights the importance of water, including health, environment, and daily uses. The text will incorporate target vocabulary (e.g., "potable," "filtration," "sanitation," "drought," "forecast," "important") and grammar structures (First conditional: "If we don't keep water clean, people will get sick."; For + verb + ing: "We use water for drinking, cooking, and cleaning."; Because + cause: "Clean water is essential because it supports life.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading comprehension of informational texts to extract key details and follow instructions for water conservation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Phonemic Awareness:</b> The teacher introduces the text by modeling pronunciation of specific words, focusing on syllabification for "forecast" (fore-cast) and "important" (im-por-tant). Students repeat the words after the teacher, breaking them into syllables.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Reading):</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Reading:</b> Students read the title and first paragraph. "What is the main idea of this text?" (Expected: "Clean water is important.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> The teacher provides 3-4 T/F statements about general facts from the text. Students read the text carefully to decide if each statement is true or false. E.g., "Clean water is only important for drinking." (False). "We use water for cooking and cleaning." (True).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases related to the purpose of water with specific uses mentioned in the text (e.g., "For health" -> "prevents sickness"; "For daily tasks" -> "washing clothes").</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension, identifying cause-effect using "if...will" and "because," expressing purpose using "for + -ing," and applying phonemic awareness for decoding two-syble and three-syllable words.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Practice - Reading for Grammar):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from the informational text. They underline all sentences that use "If...will" (first conditional) in green, and circle sentences that use "for + verb + ing" in blue. They also highlight sentences that use "because" to state a cause. Example: "If we don't save water, we will face water shortages." "We use water for drinking." "We need clean water because it is essential."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled - Reading for Details & Phonemics):</b> Students are given a list of instructions on how to filter water (e.g., "Collect rainwater in a clean bucket. Use a cloth to filter big drops. Then, boil the water carefully."). They read the instructions and then answer specific comprehension questions based on them (e.g., "What is the first step?", "Why do we boil the water?"). During this, the teacher guides students to pronounce words like "filtration" and "collect" by applying basic syllabification rules.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Pair Interaction - Peer Check Reading):</b> In pairs, students receive a short text with missing words (cloze activity). The missing words are from the target vocabulary (e.g., "potable," "resource," "conserve," "tap," "polluted"). They read the text together and collaboratively decide on the best word to fill each blank, then read their completed text aloud to each other, correcting any reading or comprehension errors. Example: "Water is a precious _____. We must _____ it daily. If our rivers are _____, the water is not _____."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Reading and Instruction Following for a Mini-Project.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a printed set of instructions for a simple "Water Conservation Challenge" at home (e.g., "How to Collect Rainwater for Plants" or "Daily Steps to Save Water at Home"). The instructions are clear, concise, and use target vocabulary (e.g., "turn off the tap," "collect rainwater," "use water wisely").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Their task is to:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Read the instructions carefully as a group.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify the key steps (extract facts).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Discuss how they would follow these instructions, explaining the purpose of each step using "for + -ing" or "because." E.g., "We turn off the tap for saving water because it's a limited resource."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Create a simple visual (e.g., a mini-poster or a sequence of drawings) to illustrate 3-4 key instructions from the text they read. The poster must use short sentences summarizing the instructions.</li>
                </ul>
                The teacher circulates, offering support, checking reading comprehension, and prompting students to use the target grammar and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment:</b> Observation checklist during group work, focusing on students' ability to read and follow instructions, extract key details, and use target vocabulary and grammar (first conditional, for + verb + ing, because) in their discussions and visual summaries. The teacher notes how well students demonstrate phonemic awareness when reading words like "important" or "forecast" within the context of the instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their mini-poster or sequence of drawings. They briefly (1-2 sentences per instruction) explain the steps they read, using language to express purpose ("for + -ing") or cause-effect ("because").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of extracted instructions/details from the text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of target vocabulary (e.g., save, waste, tap, collect, essential).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate application of grammar (first conditional, for + verb + ing, because).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrated phonemic awareness by pronouncing key multi-syllable words correctly.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative interaction within the group to complete the reading and summary task.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a small slip of paper:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I learned that clean water is important for __________."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One instruction I can follow to save water is __________."</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection, connection to next lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's reading activity was most helpful for understanding the importance of water?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I use the information I read today to help my family save water?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well today? (e.g., "Students were actively engaged in reading the instructions and identifying key steps. The phonemic awareness practice for 'important' and 'forecast' was helpful.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., "Some students struggled with the first conditional, so I need to include more guided practice with 'if...will' structures in the speaking stage. I should also provide more visual support for interpreting complex sentences.")</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 3 (Speaking & Interaction), students will use the facts and instructions they read today to discuss water conservation strategies and propose solutions in groups, expressing cause-effect and purpose actively.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>